    },
    {
      "title": "Bound the others",
      "body": "<p>For an unfamiliar logarithm, put its argument between two nearby powers of its base. For the surd power, first decide whether its base is below or above one.</p>",
      "recap": "A logarithm is the exponent needed to produce its argument.",
      "pitfall": "A high positive power does not always make a number large.",
      "pause": "Find bounds tight enough to identify the largest expression.",
      "recall": [
